(PRC-22b - device nodes with the path as a buffer and the numbers as
 variables, both accepted; "b" and "c" are refused unprivileged (EPERM,
 or EEXIST on a path already taken) and nothing appears. strace:
 mknod(path, S_IFBLK|0666, makedev(0x7, 0)) = -1 EPERM. Shape of 'gen
 leaf process device node refusal', kind 427 (process batch C,
 2026-10-05). Never type "p" (D1).
 Ran, from the repo root, on the installed vox v0.4.15:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-22b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the block node was refused
   no node appeared
   the taken path was refused
   the file is still there
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
a buffer called gizmo is "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_gizmo".
a number called 'major number' is 7.
a number called 'minor number' is 0.
Create a device node called gizmo with type "b" major 'major number' minor 'minor number'.
On error print "the block node was refused".
If gizmo is not available then, print "no node appeared".
open a file for writing called scribe at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_taken".
Write "taken" to scribe.
Close scribe.
Create a device node called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_taken" with type "c" major 1 minor 3.
On error print "the taken path was refused".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_taken" is available then, print "the file is still there".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_taken".
